+# RPi firmware CI acquisition / 2026-10-11
+
+Parent: [ws129-p015](../phase015/phase.md)
+Worktree: codex/ci-rpi-firmware, base main9a0ddc6cb. Unintegrated boot0 changes are not in this branch.
+
+## Failure evidence
+
+[CI38079321808](https://github.com/awemorris/zedBSD/actions/runs/38079321808), head402598d2708ca3ed3daaf923caedb73e6c95d2e4, failed during Build arm64: `No rule to make target 'vendor/raspberrypi-firmware/boot/start4.elf', needed by 'bootloader'`. Default actions/checkout did not initialize submodules. Gitlink pins firmware3d301dd924bcd758a4c8cb19fe8531031f033f43. Full failed-step log saved privately at build/ci-rpi-firmware/failed-run.log; read-only gh run list/view successful. No remote mutation or CI rerun.
+
+## Changes
+
+Before Build arm64, nightly now executes `git submodule update --init --depth 1 -- vendor/raspberrypi-firmware`. The pinned gitlink remains unchanged; upstream HEAD is not adopted. .gitmodules also records shallow=true for this submodule. No recursive/all-submodule acquisition is added. The RPi artifact now compresses build/arm64/hdd-image.img rather than build/amd64/hdd-image.img. Tagged release currently builds amd64 only and is unchanged.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+- PyYAML parsed the changed workflow; `bash -n` passed for every build-job run step. Diff-check PASS. Existing YAML indentation and simple run syntax preserved. Full applicable AGENTS/Guardrail/project-rule review performed; no C source change or separate YAML/shell full standard is present.
+- Small isolated Git fixture under build/ci-rpi-firmware/shallow-3a4ugwd9 creates three firmware revisions, pins the second in a parent gitlink, and substitutes only the fixture file:// URL into the actual .gitmodules. It executes the exact command extracted from the changed workflow. Checked out HEAD equals the older pin, `git rev-parse --is-shallow-repository` is true, all fixture boot payloads are present and start4.elf has revision2 content. A repeat command succeeds and preserves the pin. Production/shared submodule and Git configuration are untouched.
+- Source diff confirms unchanged production gitlink, one targeted depth1 acquisition, correct arm64 artifact input and unchanged amd64/tagged-release behavior.
+- No full firmware network transfer, toolchain/image rebuild, remote Actions run/success, long monitoring, push or release publication. The fixture verifies Git semantics, not GitHub network availability or subsequent unrelated compilation. User previously requested no long CI monitoring; none is started.
+
+Limited workflow/host criteria cleared. Main/push require the concrete change's approval; shared Master/Queue/history/cache/GitHub planning projections remain Q1 pending. WS release acceptance remains incomplete.
